  "notes": "Cash basis county, governmental funds only (no business-type funds). Statement lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4). Cash and fund balance kept separate: ending cash = Cash and Cash Equivalents 11,840,758 (p3; investments printed '-'); beginning cash not printed (fund balance 11,582,536 p4 recorded as beginning_fund_balance). Fund-balance roll-forward: 11,582,536 + 10,022,988 - 9,764,766 + 3,390,030 - 3,390,030 = 11,840,758. Balance sheet from the governmental funds statement p3 (totals equal the Statement of Net Position p1). Taxes 4,370,694 has no printed tax-type breakdown (Statement of Activities prints only 'Taxes'), kept as one line. Bond Fund budget schedule prints Taxes 122 / Intergovernmental 1,530,377 while the p4 Bond Fund column prints 123 / 1,530,376 (same total 1,530,499); schedule lines recorded as printed. Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p5); Road, Buyback, Inheritance Tax and Bond Fund budget schedules (pp6-7; disbursements printed as one line); nonmajor funds from the combining statement (pp12-15, more detailed than the one-line nonmajor budget schedules pp8-11, which are not recorded to avoid double counting). Zero-actual lines (Buyback disbursements, Vets Aid, County/Federal Drug Law funds) omitted. Lottery/Keno Fund receipts are printed as Intergovernmental and kept as state aid (no printed keno evidence). Read pages 1-15 of 15"
}
